WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.000
Every step, done for real. Use the chapters to jump to any part.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.357
You need two free apps: VS Code and Node.js.

3
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:13.884
In VS Code, open the terminal: View, then Terminal.

4
00:00:13.884 --> 00:00:18.969
Type node -v and press Enter. Version 20.9 or newer is fine.

5
00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:22.475
Go to the folder where you keep projects and run this command.

6
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:27.624
It makes a new Next.js project called my-app, with Tailwind CSS set up.

7
00:00:27.624 --> 00:00:33.224
Installing takes a minute or two. We fast-forward through it.

8
00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:37.285
Done. Warnings about vulnerabilities are normal for a new project.

9
00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:40.428
Now move into the new folder: type cd my-app.

10
00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:45.022
Then open the my-app folder in VS Code: File, then Open Folder.

11
00:00:45.022 --> 00:00:48.699
This is your project. Everything you add goes into src.

12
00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:54.317
Nexus UI installs with the shadcn CLI. Set it up once per project.

13
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:58.117
-d uses the default settings, so it asks you nothing.

14
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:02.796
It adds components.json, the settings file the CLI reads.

15
00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:08.371
And src/lib/utils.ts, the small cn() helper every component uses.

16
00:01:08.371 --> 00:01:13.392
Now tell the CLI where Nexus UI lives. Copy this command as it is.

17
00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:17.666
Keep {name} exactly like that. The CLI fills it in for you.

18
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:24.266
It adds one entry to components.json. You do this once per project.

19
00:01:24.266 --> 00:01:28.647
Every component page has an Install box. Copy the command from it.

20
00:01:28.647 --> 00:01:33.047
Paste it in the terminal. Here we add the Glow Button, which is free.

21
00:01:33.047 --> 00:01:37.449
It downloads the files and installs what they need, like framer-motion.

22
00:01:37.449 --> 00:01:42.049
The new files are in src/components/glow-button.

23
00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:46.686
Open src/app/page.tsx. This file is your home page.

24
00:01:46.686 --> 00:01:52.486
Replace what's there: import the component, then put it on the page.

25
00:01:52.486 --> 00:01:56.035
Save the file, then start the app with npm run dev.

26
00:01:56.035 --> 00:01:59.477
Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser.

27
00:01:59.477 --> 00:02:03.677
There it is: the Glow Button, running in your own project.

28
00:02:03.677 --> 00:02:09.477
Point at it and the light on the rim turns to face you.

29
00:02:09.477 --> 00:02:13.538
Prefer not to use the CLI? Copy the code by hand instead.

30
00:02:13.538 --> 00:02:18.338
First, install the packages the component needs.

31
00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:23.738
Then press Show the source files. Each tab is one file, with its path.

32
00:02:23.738 --> 00:02:26.538
Copy the code from each tab.

33
00:02:26.538 --> 00:02:30.855
In VS Code, create the file at that exact path and paste the code.

34
00:02:30.855 --> 00:02:36.110
Do this for every tab, including ui-sounds.ts. Then use it in a page.

35
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.710
Pro components need a Pro plan and an API key from your dashboard.

36
00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:45.510
Create a file called .env.local in your project and put your key in it.

37
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:51.171
In components.json, change the registries entry so the CLI sends your key.

38
00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.771
Then add Pro components the same way as free ones.

39
00:02:55.371 --> 00:03:00.271
Each of these starts from a project set up in steps 1 to 4.

40
00:03:00.271 --> 00:03:05.356
Blocks install exactly like components. Copy the command from the block's page.

41
00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:10.556
Here is the free Pricing Section.

42
00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:16.515
The block's Code view has a "2. Use it" snippet. Paste it into src/app/page.tsx.

43
00:03:16.515 --> 00:03:23.715
Your pricing section, live. Pick a plan and everything updates.

44
00:03:23.715 --> 00:03:28.053
Icons are single files. Free ones can be fetched with one command.

45
00:03:28.053 --> 00:03:31.495
Make a folder for them, then download the icon into it.

46
00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:36.132
Icons animate with Framer Motion, so install it if you don't have it yet.

47
00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:39.932
Import the icon and use it like any component.

48
00:03:39.932 --> 00:03:46.332
Point at the bell: it winds up, swings and rings.

49
00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:50.329
Sounds are made in the browser, so there are no audio files to add.

50
00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:55.798
One command adds src/lib/ui-sounds.ts, the whole free sound library.

51
00:03:55.798 --> 00:04:01.598
Call playSound with a name from the Sounds page, here "pop".

52
00:04:01.598 --> 00:04:08.198
Click it and you hear the pop. Turn your sound on.

53
00:04:08.198 --> 00:04:13.752
Free videos: Launch Reel, Kinetic Manifesto and Will Return. Open the Source tab.

54
00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:22.719
Make a folder src/app/video-frame. Save the video, kit.ts and frame.tsx (as page.tsx) in it.

55
00:04:22.719 --> 00:04:30.449
Put the images it imports in an assets folder next to them, from nexus-ui.com/videos/assets.

56
00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:34.936
Install Playwright once. You also need ffmpeg on your computer.

57
00:04:34.936 --> 00:04:42.367
Start the app with npm run dev, then run render.mjs. It draws every frame and adds the music.

58
00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:49.367
Your MP4, rendered on your own machine.

59
00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:53.967
Sign in (a free account is enough), then press Download source (.zip).

60
00:04:53.967 --> 00:04:57.985
Unzip it where you keep projects and open the folder in VS Code.

61
00:04:57.985 --> 00:05:01.982
It's a complete Next.js project, so install its packages.

62
00:05:01.982 --> 00:05:06.149
Start it with npm run dev. The README has every step too.

63
00:05:06.149 --> 00:05:15.149
Launchfolio, running on your machine. Edit the copy and make it yours.

64
00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:20.149
That's it. Your project is ready for anything from Nexus UI.

65
00:05:20.149 --> 00:05:26.535
The written guide with every command is at nexus-ui.com/docs/installation.
